# BATMAN!

Smash cut to the 1960s Batman title card.

Don't start with the Batman instrumental. Start with eight different people saying “new,” all perfectly timed to the Batman melody.

By the sixth “new,” the audience recognises the pattern. On the eighth, the real Batman theme kicks in and you smash cut to Batman.

Then Batman says something completely unrelated, perhaps “No,” and we're back in the phonetic montage.

## 2. NU NU NU NU NU NU — DARUDE SANDSTORM

This should be a musical escalation gag.

Start with actual snippets of people saying “nu,” “new,” “noob,” or “noo.” Repeat them faster and faster. Gradually introduce the rhythm and timbre of Sandstorm beneath the chopped vocal samples.

Then drop every spoken voice at once and reveal the unmistakable synth hook.

The extra joke: flash the classic internet question “song name?” followed by “Darude – Sandstorm”, referencing the old meme.

