### Editing it so the joke lands

I'd make each recurring musical gag a little more intrusive. The first Batman transition lasts two seconds. The second one lasts half a second, because the viewer already knows what's coming. The third time, just the first three rhythmic “new”s should be enough to make them anticipate Batman—and then you deny them the payoff.

For the sound design, use each source clip as a sample: trim it tightly around “new,” quantise the syllable onsets to the rhythm, lightly pitch-shift where necessary, and use short crossfades to avoid clicks. Keep enough of the original voices and background noise for the source changes to remain funny.

One last idea: Darude – Sandstorm is itself the famous joke answer to “What song is this?”&#x20;

